From 63f4fab04289db6111909438071c5732612bcbdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 10:37:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.x (1.13.10): dtor position, sig-checked overrides, O3
 drop glue, MSVC ??_G, doc comments
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five fixes from the v1.13.10 review campaign:

1. Dtor slot position (HIGH): the D1/D0 pair sits at the destructor's
   DECLARATION position (Itanium §2.5.2), not pinned first. New
   positional `slot=~dtor,~` attr record (parse_imported_slots ->
   CxxVtSlot::ImportedDtorPair) expanded in place by both vtable
   emitters; legacy `vdtor=1`-only attrs keep the prepend semantics
   (correct exactly when the dtor was declared first). `~op<N>`
   placeholder records preserve operator-virtual slot indices.

2. Signature-checked overrides: `slot=` records carry an optional
   third field — the Itanium bare parameter encoding at the declaring
   class. virtuals_on_chain matches name+params (disambiguating
   OVERLOADED base virtuals, which name-only matching silently
   corrupted) and rejects ABI-incompatible overrides with a real
   diagnostic instead of emitting a mis-typed slot.

3. Drop-glue at -C opt-level>=1: instantiation_mode now forces
   GloballyShared (COMDAT) for the drop glue of #[repr(cpp)] classes
   whose chain has a virtual dtor — the C++ vtable references the glue
   BY SYMBOL (a codegen-time reference MIR-based LocalCopy placement
   can't see), which left it undefined at link time. The collector
   root also visits the drop use as INDIRECT, like trait-object
   vtable entries.

4. MSVC ??_G: the scalar-deleting-dtor thunk (and the exported ??_G
   trampoline) now honor the flags argument — bit 0 gates `operator
   delete`, so virtual destruction WITHOUT deallocation (`p->~T()`
   through a base pointer) no longer frees storage it doesn't own.

5. class-body parser: `///` doc comments on methods no longer trip
   "fields must appear before methods" — the member lookahead skips
   DocComment tokens, and the keyword-modifier path consumes them
   into #[doc] attrs grafted onto the parsed method.

Vendored rustc_abi_cxx gains mangle_itanium_params (the bare param
encoding used for override checking).
---
 compiler/rustc_abi_cxx/src/mangle.rs          |  12 ++
 compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/cxx_vtable.rs |  87 +++++++++++--
 compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/mono_item.rs  |  53 ++++++--
 compiler/rustc_middle/src/mono.rs             |  45 +++++++
 compiler/rustc_monomorphize/src/collector.rs  |  10 +-
 compiler/rustc_parse/src/parser/item.rs       |  33 ++++-
 compiler/rustc_passes/src/check_attr.rs       |   5 +-
 compiler/rustc_symbol_mangling/src/itanium.rs | 121 ++++++++++++++++--
 8 files changed, 330 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)

diff --git a/compiler/rustc_abi_cxx/src/mangle.rs b/compiler/rustc_abi_cxx/src/mangle.rs
index 2dd7515c308..bd34e735ccb 100644
--- a/compiler/rustc_abi_cxx/src/mangle.rs
+++ b/compiler/rustc_abi_cxx/src/mangle.rs
@@ -99,6 +99,18 @@ pub fn mangle_itanium(&self, sym: &Symbol) -> String {
         m.mangle_symbol(sym);
         m.out
     }
+
+    /// The Itanium *bare parameter encoding* of a function signature —
+    /// the `<params>` tail of `_ZN…E<params>` (`"v"` for an empty
+    /// list, e.g. `"iPKc"` for `(int, const char*)`). v1.13.10: used
+    /// to signature-check `override fn`s against the `slot=` records'
+    /// third field. Substitution state is local to this call,
+    /// matching a standalone declaration's encoding.
+    pub fn mangle_itanium_params(&self, sig: &crate::ty::FnSig) -> String {
+        let mut m = Mangler::new(self);
+        m.emit_params(&sig.params);
+        m.out
+    }
 }
 
